                "text": "Analyse the examples:\n- Example 1:\n  - Input contains several shapes and noise pixels.\n  - Shapes of size 3x3:\n    - 4: hollow 3x3 at rows 5-7, cols 1-3. (Also extra pixel (1,2) of color 4? Yes, a noise pixel 4 at (1,2)).\n    - 2: hollow 3x3 at rows 1-3, cols 6-8? Row 3 has 2,2,2,2 (extra pixel at col 9).\n    - 7: hollow 3x3 at rows 4-6, cols 11-13.\n    - Output is 3x3 squares stitched together horizontally: [4, 2, 7].\n    - Wait, 4 is at x=1..3, 2 is at x=6..8, 7 is at x=11..13?\n    - Output order: 4, then 2, then 7. (Ordered by left-to-right? 4 is at col 1, 2 is at col 6, 7 is at col 11. Yes!)\n    - Size: 3x3 each. Total size 3x9.\n- Example 2:\n  - Input contains 4x4 squares:\n    - 1: 4x4 solid square at rows 4-7, cols 1-4. (Row 6 col 0 is an extra pixel of 1).\n    - 9: 4x4 solid square at rows 5-8, cols 7-10.\n    - 6: 4x4 solid square at rows 0-3, cols 12-15. (Row 4 col 14 is extra pixel of 6).\n    - Output has 1, 9, 6! Ordered left to right: 1 (col 1), 9 (col 7), 6 (col 12).\n    - Size: 4x4 each, total size 4x12.\n- Example 3:\n  - Shapes:\n    - 2: 3x3 hollow square.\n    - 4: 3x3 hollow square.\n    - 3: 5x5 hollow square at rows 5-9, cols 1-5.\n    - 8: 5x5 hollow square at rows 1-5, cols 8-12. (Row 3 col 13 is extra pixel).\n    - Output has 3 and 8! Both are 5x5 hollow squares.\n    - Wait! Why 3 and 8, and not 2 and 4?\n    - Notice size: 3 and 8 are 5x5! Are they the largest square frames?\n    - In Example 1: 4, 2, 7 are 3x3. There are no larger squares.\n    - In Example 2: 1, 9, 6 are 4x4.\n    - So we find the largest squares (or most frequent size of square? Or largest size? In Ex 3, largest size is 5x5, while 3x3 also exist. Output keeps only the largest squares!).\n    - And cleans up any extra/noise pixels outside the perfect square/frame.\n    - Ordered from left to right (by column of the square).Analyse the rule:\n1. Identify all squares (solid or hollow frames of size $N \\times N$, with border thickness 1, possibly with some noise pixels attached or scattered).\n2. Consider the largest size $N$ that appears.\n3. Extract all clean $N \\times N$ squares of this largest size.\n4. Concatenate them horizontally ordered from left to right (by their x / column coordinate).\n\nPlease provide the first test input grid.",
